module examples.err_layout_runtime_cycle

# plans/M10.md item A2: nesting is recursive, so it can be circular, and a
# circular one has no finite size. `Mailbox` nests `TurnArea`, which nests
# `Mailbox` again — a transitive cycle, deliberately not the trivial
# `struct A: a: A`, because the trivial one can be caught by a single
# equality test that a two-step loop walks straight past.
#
# The requirement is not merely "rejected": it is rejected *as a
# diagnostic*, before the recursion runs, naming the whole chain. A
# compiler pass that answered this with a stack overflow would be reporting
# a bug in itself, which is the failure mode `internal error:` exists to
# make visible and this rejection exists to prevent.

@layout(runtime, endian=little)
struct Mailbox:
    head: u32
    slot: TurnArea


@layout(runtime, endian=little)
struct TurnArea:
    state: u32
    owner: Mailbox
